 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Cool. Reunions are always fun. Whoever you ask though, it's typical to get yawns. Is there travel that opens up at last? A city to stay in together? Then ask the family which ones you can reach by video call first, so you have them before the travel. Whichever ones are arriving late. Not necessarily, though it looks nice at the door. A few basic dishes you know everyone likes, and a few snacks. Good idea. Ask the guests to bring a veg, a cheese, and a drink if they can. Keeps costs down and makes it feel more shared. Keep it simple for now. Names and roughly when people arrive. You can ask each guest to confirm later.",
